# The README's hero: open atlas-web and relay-cli from the `+` dropdown and launch one session in
# each (one finishes unread, one stops on a permission prompt), then back to orbit-api for four
# launches across two checkouts — two into feat/auth-tokens through the box's ^T worktree picker
# (a Codex one that finishes unread, a Claude one that opens a pull request and keeps running),
# two into main (one stopped on a prompt, an OpenCode one finished and read) — a terminal in
# main, then out to the bands with the cursor on feat/auth-tokens, the pane reading its running
# session.
#
# The pane edge is dragged up right after the first launch — the grab zone is the grid row over
# the pane's rule — so every later session is spawned into the taller pane and its transcript
# fits. A 0.6 s `sleep` after each launch and each project open lets it settle before the next key
# (a `p` pressed while a launch is still landing is lost and the task types as hotkeys), and the
# long one at the end lets the PR sweep and the delayed finishes land. They are waits with no key,
# so none is typed into a session that has the keys, or left in the KEY COMBO DISPLAY. The
# stand-in's unread finishes are posted 10–16 s after their launch, once the keys have moved on,
# so they land while the later boxes are being typed. The OpenCode launch is six rows down the
# box's harness picker, past Grok Build.
+
atlas
Enter
sleep 0.6
p
Migrate the checkout page to the new design tokens
Enter
sleep 0.6
drag 95 33 95 24
+
relay
Enter
sleep 0.6
p
Add a --json flag to every list command
Enter
sleep 0.6
+
orbit
Enter
sleep 0.6
p
C-t
auth
Enter
sleep 0.6
Write integration tests for token expiry and refresh
Tab
Down
Enter
Enter
sleep 0.6
p
Move the token store from a JSON file to sqlite
Enter
sleep 0.6
p
C-t
Up
